<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Levan II Dadiani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1591–1657</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Levan II Dadiani was prince of Mingrelia in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1611 to 1657. He made Mingrelia the strongest power in western Georgia, warring against the kingdom of Imereti and the princes of Guria and Abkhazia. His court was described by the Italian missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcangelo-lamberti">Arcangelo Lamberti</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> with Ottoman ports was a large part of his revenues.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/levan-ii-dadiani.jpg" alt="Levan II Dadiani" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Levan_II_Dadaini_mural.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
